  "candidate_bridge": "For a mixed/secant matrix M whose columns lie in convex hulls of kernel-derivative curves, replace one column by its maximizing endpoint. The exact inverse difference is rank one: K(M_new)-K(M_old)=-[e1^T M_new^-1*(column_new-column_old)]*(M_old^-1 v)_j. Uniform curvature and inverse-direction signs would make each of 21 replacements nondecreasing. With all other columns fixed, the numerator of (M^-1 v)_12 is independent of column 12 by Cramers rule, and the determinant sign is constant on the connected nonsingular column family, so a single reference sign could resolve the final coordinate. This bridge requires a dedicated complete proof and independent audit.",
